THOUGHT: To fix the new NullAway error, I should make writeArgType handle a possibly null inner type safely. Since it already treats a null argType by writing -1, I can mirror that behavior for a null inner type: check if getInnerType() is null and, if so, write -1 instead of recursing. This avoids passing a @Nullable value where @NonNull is required and preserves serialization semantics.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/jadx && sed -i '282,286s/} else if (argType.getOuterType() != null) {/} else if (argType.getOuterType() != null) {
			ArgType innerType = argType.getInnerType();
			if (innerType == null) {
				out.writeByte(TypeEnum.OUTER_GENERIC.ordinal());
				writeArgType(out, argType.getOuterType(), names);
				out.writeByte(-1);
				return;
			}/' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/clsp/ClsSet.java && sed -i '285s/writeArgType(out, argType.getInnerType(), names);/writeArgType(out, innerType, names);/' jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/clsp/ClsSet.java && nl -ba jadx-core/src/main/java/jadx/core/clsp/ClsSet.java | sed -n '274,292p' && ./gradlew jadx-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 || true && grep -n "getInnerType()" new_build_output.log || true && tail -n 40 new_build_output.log
```

